# Hash-pinned operational scripts must land on disk byte-for-byte.
#
# `keepalive.ps1` refuses to start the runtime unless `start.ps1` hashes to a
# pinned SHA-256 (`32310769...`, see tools/runtime/runtime-root/README.md). This
# repository runs with `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. That single rewrite changes the bytes, breaks the pin, and leaves the
# runtime unable to start -- a failure that first appears on a machine that has
# never run the script, long after the commit that caused it.
#
# `text eol=lf` writes these paths as LF on every checkout, so the working copy
# matches the committed blob exactly. It is preferred over `-text` because git
# keeps treating the files as text: diffs, blame and merges still work.
tools/runtime/runtime-root/*.ps1 text eol=lf
